  "reveal": {
    "brief_voiced": "Effie Strange stands as the killer. The Colonel's tradition demands a loaded pistol at every place, yet no pistol at any seat beside a lady shall remain charged. Lady Lavinia Loveless sat at the third place upon the host's right, with Effie Strange at the fourth place upon that same side. The charged pistol lay at Lady Lavinia's place—a breach of protocol that placed the weapon within Effie's reach, along the clear length of the side between them.\n\nEffie Strange is known to be clever where the company finds her uncomfortable, spendthrift, and always short of money. Lady Lavinia Loveless, a faded actress turned medium, is apt to let people rather too close. One reads in this the opening: a woman of wit and want, in proximity to one whose nature invites confidence, and whose loose regard for propriety left her vulnerable to a neighbour's design.\n\nThe file closes upon a murder staged within the Colonel's own rules, turned inside out by a woman who understood them too well.",
